WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.533
Hi, I'm Sprocket!

00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:05.432
Qwen3.8-Omni-Flash reads text, images, audio and video.

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:09.988
Its real news is that it doesn't watch the whole video.

00:00:11.308 --> 00:00:14.934
Instead of ingesting a whole recording, the model starts from the question,

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:17.955
and decides for itself what to watch and listen to.

00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:24.188
Static ingestion samples the whole file at a fixed rate, so cost

00:00:24.188 --> 00:00:25.423
grows with video length.

00:00:25.843 --> 00:00:29.967
Agentic perception plans what to sample, one function call at a time,

00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:31.342
conditioned on the question.

00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:35.449
It begins with the question, and picks a stretch of the

00:00:35.449 --> 00:00:36.366
recording to look at.

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:40.449
Only that span is sampled, frames and sound, and what it finds

00:00:40.449 --> 00:00:41.669
is kept as evidence.

00:00:42.089 --> 00:00:45.453
If that isn't enough, it zooms in and looks again, round after

00:00:45.453 --> 00:00:46.574
round, coarse to fine.

00:00:46.994 --> 00:00:49.353
When the evidence answers the question, it stops.

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:51.418
Most of the video is never read.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:58.139
On OmniVideoBench, that spent forty-five point seven percent fewer tokens, and accuracy

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:01.957
rose from sixty-three point four to sixty-seven point eight.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:07.800
A live stream goes two ways: a vision encoder, and Spatial AuT,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.049
a new audio transformer that locates targets by sound.

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:14.328
Both feed the Thinker, which reasons and writes text.

00:01:14.328 --> 00:01:16.870
Its wait grows as the input gets longer.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.445
A separate Talker speaks the text.

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:23.756
In Qwen's latency table, that stage adds a near-fixed three hundred fifty-six

00:01:23.756 --> 00:01:25.552
to four hundred eight milliseconds.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.460
Choosing what to watch isn't a quality-for-speed trade.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.049
On this benchmark it was cheaper and more accurate at once.

00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:39.283
To recap: start from the question, zoom in only where needed, and

00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:40.550
split thinking from talking.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.115
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:43.115 --> 00:01:43.727
I'm Sprocket.

00:01:43.727 --> 00:01:44.034
Bye!
